Inclusion Criteria:

1. Children aged 7 to 18 years who are able to swallow capsules;
2. Children with a pathological diagnosis of IgA nephropathy (IgAN) or IgA vasculitis nephritis (IgAVN);
3. Children meeting any one of the following criteria A, B, C, or D: A. Progressive IgA nephropathy with indications for corticosteroid therapy, defined by meeting any one of the following (a-e): a. MEST-C score of 0 but urine protein-to-creatinine ratio (UPCR) \> 2 g/g; b. Active MEST-C score (defined by at least one of the following: M1, E1, S1 with podocyte lesions, or C1) and UPCR of 0.5-1 g/g, with persistent proteinuria despite 3 months of renin-angiotensin system blocker (RASB) therapy; c. Active MEST-C score (defined by at least one of the following: M1, E1, S1 with podocyte lesions, or C1) and UPCR \> 1 g/g, with persistent proteinuria despite 1 month of RASB therapy; d. Active MEST-C score (defined by at least one of the following: M1, E1, S1 with podocyte lesions, or C1) accompanied by nephrotic-range proteinuria; e. Rapidly progressive glomerulonephritis or C2 lesions. Note: Concomitant use of immunosuppressants is permitted for children with nephrotic-range proteinuria accompanied by active MEST-C lesions. B. Pediatric patients with IgAVN presenting with non-nephrotic-range proteinuria or pathological grade IIb or IIIa, who have received ACEI/ARB therapy and have a glomerular filtration rate (GFR) \> 50 mL/min/1.73 m². Note: Concomitant use of immunosuppressants is permitted for treatment-naïve patients with pathological grade ≥ III, crescent formation ≥ 25%, clinical presentation of massive proteinuria, or declining renal function. C. Patients with IgAV or IgAVN who have had a suboptimal response to corticosteroid and immunosuppressive therapy. D. Patients with recurrent episodes of macroscopic hematuria whose parents strongly desire to control the disease.
4. Estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) ≥ 30 mL/min/1.73 m² at enrollment, calculated using the Schwartz formula (0.413 × 88.4 × height \[cm\] / serum creatinine \[μmol/L\]);
5. Willingness to sign the informed consent form.

Exclusion Criteria:

1. Presence of active infections requiring antiviral or antibiotic therapy;
2. Patients with uncontrolled severe hypertension or diabetes;
3. Individuals with other autoimmune diseases, primary immunodeficiency, or malignancies;
4. History of organ transplantation;
5. Presence of chronic active infections (e.g., Epstein-Barr virus, cytomegalovirus, or Mycobacterium tuberculosis) where the use of corticosteroids and immunosuppressants may exacerbate the disease;
6. Patients with severe hepatic impairment, heart failure, or end-stage renal disease (ESRD);
7. Any other medical condition that may place the patient at increased risk due to participation in this study;
8. Patients deemed unsuitable for participation by the investigator.

Note: The historical comparator participants are identified retrospectively from medical records under a waiver of informed consent approved by the institutional review board; all other eligibility criteria apply to them as well, and they must not have received budesonide before or during the index treatment period.
